<p>A strike on Al Deain Teaching Hospital in al-Daein, the capital of East Darfur state, killed 64 people and wounded 89 on Friday, according to the World Health Organization and multiple news reports published Saturday. WHO Director-General Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said the dead included 13 children. AllAfrica’s WHO statement added that those killed included two female nurses, one male doctor, and multiple patients. The strike left the teaching hospital nonfunctional, adding to the strain on health care in a country already devastated by war. UN humanitarian officials said they were appalled by the attack and pointed to the heavy civilian toll, while Tedros condemned it and called for de-escalation and stronger protection for civilians and health care.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9TYclpQxTRGvgRUoAJQ2A_RKsAJ0cJ6qfr6n_r4pB27kgGghyanEPMVumdSgSg4jrZvUu0iUHacnBbHMkiUBBUWIo_-wl5pjzV7mmYY9XNkUBKFo60Ahoc2UvIawfBLm4PbjlpHwZ2ZWvDlSXkw7OsVTbMDtE92tVcv9arDCJgd3_eZiiH3Qk-zR1Dj8jx5v262_u3Ah8OcmyMifedJ1j8vy5nZ9Zgv3x9b3b26c-_xOTaY73I5fTSI1Xi7sqLbuy-8QeZwHJzn9nlE' alt='Image accompanying coverage of the strike on Al Deain Teaching Hospital in East Darfur' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Local monitoring: The Sudanese rights group Emergency Lawyers documented the attack, showing how local monitors helped bring details from East Darfur to light.</li><li>Reported method: The Guardian described the incident as an army drone attack, adding a reported weapon and attribution detail beyond WHO’s casualty update.</li><li>Response sequence: The UN humanitarian office in Sudan raised the alarm first, before WHO published the fuller casualty toll on Saturday.</li></ul><blockquote>@WHO has verified yet another attack on health care in #Sudan. - Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>World Health Organization: Tedros used the strike to press for stronger protection for civilians and medical services, treating the safety of health care itself as a central concern. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603210068.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>UN humanitarian office in Sudan: The UN aid office’s statement served as an early humanitarian alert from East Darfur, drawing attention to the immediate civilian toll after the strike. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/21/strike-on-sudan-hospital-kills-wounds-world-health-organization-reports'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Emergency Lawyers: International coverage’s reliance on the Sudanese rights group underscored how local civil society monitors help surface allegations and casualty information during the war. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3347452/64-killed-including-13-children-attack-sudan-hospital-who-says'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3347452/64-killed-including-13-children-attack-sudan-hospital-who-says'>64 killed – including 13 children – in attack on Sudan hospital, WHO says</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-over-60-killed-in-strike-on-hospital-who-says/a-76471162'>Sudan: Over 60 killed in strike on hospital, WHO says</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/21/strike-on-sudan-hospital-kills-wounds-world-health-organization-reports'>Strike on Sudan hospital kills at least 64 and wounds 89 more, WHO reports</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202603210068.html'>Sudan: Dr Tedros Condemns Attack on Sudan Hospital, Cals for De-escalation and Civilian Protections</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/21/who-says-attack-on-sudan-hospital-killed-64-including-13-children'>WHO says attack on Sudan hospital killed 64, including 13 children</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/64-killed-in-attack-on-sudan-healthcare-facility-who/article70770486.ece'>64 killed in attack on 